# Maintainer keys trusted to sign release tags.
#
# publish.yaml runs `git verify-tag` on every pushed `v*` tag against THIS
# file as it exists on `main` (never the copy inside the tag being checked,
# so a tag cannot vouch for itself). An unsigned tag, or one signed by a key
# not listed here, never reaches pub.dev.
#
# Format (one line per key; see `man ssh-keygen`, "ALLOWED SIGNERS"):
#
#   <tagger email> namespaces="git" <key type> <public key>
#
# e.g.
#
#   maintainer@uqpay.com namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nza...
#
# The email must equal the tagger email git records (`git config user.email`
# when the tag is made). Add or remove keys only through a reviewed PR to
# main.
#
# Maintainer setup, once per machine:
#
#   git config --global gpg.format ssh
#   git config --global user.signingkey ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
#   # then append your PUBLIC key line here, in a PR.
#
# Cutting a release:
#
#   git tag -s v1.2.3 -m "uqpay_sdk_flutter 1.2.3"   # -s = signed
#   git -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=.github/allowed_signers verify-tag v1.2.3
#   git push origin v1.2.3
#
# NO KEYS ARE LISTED YET: until a maintainer adds one, every tag is refused.
